From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:34:15 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Plutonium: the browser panel on Plutonium's browser tabs

In the Plutonium shell (navigator.windowBroker with tabs), T3's browser
works without Electron:

- plutonium/previewBridge.ts implements DesktopPreviewBridge on the
  broker's tabs, tagged with their thread id. What a page opens loads in
  the same tab, as in Electron. A reload of the shell adopts its tabs.
- plutonium/PlutoniumBrowserHost.tsx shows each session's tab with a
  SurfaceEmbed <embed> where the panel or mini player wants it, at the
  session's viewport (scaled to fit), invisibly while automation runs in
  the background, and draws the page's alert/confirm/prompt.
- plutonium/previewAutomation.ts: agent automation (status, snapshot,
  click, type, press, scroll, evaluate, waitFor) over the broker's
  DevTools passthrough; lookups run in an isolated world. Locators: CSS,
  text=, role=[name=], xpath, id=, data-testid=, >> chains, nth=.
- previewBridge, isPreviewSupportedInRuntime and PreviewAutomationHosts
  accept the Plutonium shell; the automation host also finds <embed>s.

Not yet: zoom, color scheme, element picking, screenshots to file,
recording, picture-in-picture windows, cookie import, DevTools window.

